.docname {Telemetry Types}
.docauthor {BakingRL}
.include {docs}
.doclang {en}

The SDK exports typed Rocket League telemetry event names, payload shapes, and
mock frames for local tests.

```ts
import {
  RL_TELEMETRY_EVENT_NAMES,
  isBakingRLEvent,
  telemetryFrameTemplate,
  mockGoalScored,
  type RlTelemetryEventName,
  type RlTelemetryPayloadByEvent
} from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";
```

## Event Frame Shape

Telemetry frames use the same shape as BakingRL event callbacks:

```ts
type BakingRLEvent<TData = unknown, TEvent extends string = string> = {
  Event: TEvent;
  Data: TData;
};
```

For known Rocket League events, `BakingRLEventData<TEvent>` maps the event name
to the payload type in `RlTelemetryPayloadByEvent`.

```ts
context.bus.subscribe("GoalScored", (event) => {
  event.Data.Scorer.Name;
  event.Data.GoalSpeed;
});
```

Unknown event names are typed as `unknown`, which is useful for
plugin-defined events such as `plugin.com.example.package.state`.

`context.telemetryHub.snapshot()` and `context.telemetryHub.getSnapshot()`
return the latest host-owned telemetry frame known by BakingRL, or `null` when
no Rocket League frame has been received yet. Extensions and webviews
share the same frame shape.

```ts
const frame = await context.telemetryHub.snapshot<"UpdateState">();

if (isBakingRLEvent(frame, "UpdateState")) {
  frame.Data.Game.TimeSeconds;
}
```

`isBakingRLEvent(value, eventName?)` is a small runtime guard for code that
receives an unknown frame or a nullable snapshot.

## Supported Event Names

`RL_TELEMETRY_EVENT_NAMES` contains:

- `UpdateState`
- `BallHit`
- `ClockUpdatedSeconds`
- `CountdownBegin`
- `CrossbarHit`
- `GoalReplayEnd`
- `GoalReplayStart`
- `GoalReplayWillEnd`
- `GoalScored`
- `MatchCreated`
- `MatchInitialized`
- `MatchDestroyed`
- `MatchEnded`
- `MatchPaused`
- `MatchUnpaused`
- `PodiumStart`
- `ReplayCreated`
- `ReplayWillEnd`
- `RoundStarted`
- `StatfeedEvent`

## Common Payload Types

`RlLocation`

```ts
{
  X: number;
  Y: number;
  Z: number;
}
```

`RlPlayerRef`

```ts
{
  Name: string;
  Shortcut?: number;
  TeamNum: number;
}
```

`RlPlayer` extends `RlPlayerRef` with optional scoreboard, car, boost, speed,
touch, and demolition fields such as `Score`, `Goals`, `Shots`, `Saves`,
`Boost`, `Speed`, `bOnGround`, and `bDemolished`.

`RlTeam`

```ts
{
  Name: string;
  TeamNum: number;
  Score: number;
  ColorPrimary: string;
  ColorSecondary: string;
}
```

`RlGameState` includes teams, match time, overtime state, replay state, winner
state, arena, target player, and ball state.

## Event Payload Map

`UpdateState`

Payload type: `RlUpdateStatePayload`.

Important fields:

- `MatchGuid?`
- `Players`
- `Game`

`BallHit`

Payload type: `RlBallHitPayload`.

Important fields:

- `MatchGuid?`
- `Players`
- `Ball.PreHitSpeed`
- `Ball.PostHitSpeed`
- `Ball.Location`

`ClockUpdatedSeconds`

Payload type: `RlClockUpdatedSecondsPayload`.

Important fields:

- `MatchGuid?`
- `TimeSeconds`
- `bOvertime`

Simple match events

Payload type: `RlSimpleMatchPayload`.

Events:

- `CountdownBegin`
- `GoalReplayEnd`
- `GoalReplayStart`
- `GoalReplayWillEnd`
- `MatchCreated`
- `MatchInitialized`
- `MatchDestroyed`
- `MatchPaused`
- `MatchUnpaused`
- `PodiumStart`
- `ReplayCreated`
- `ReplayWillEnd`
- `RoundStarted`

Important fields:

- `MatchGuid?`

`CrossbarHit`

Payload type: `RlCrossbarHitPayload`.

Important fields:

- `MatchGuid?`
- `BallLocation`
- `BallSpeed`
- `ImpactForce`
- `BallLastTouch`

`GoalScored`

Payload type: `RlGoalScoredPayload`.

Important fields:

- `MatchGuid?`
- `GoalSpeed`
- `GoalTime`
- `ImpactLocation`
- `Scorer`
- `Assister?`
- `BallLastTouch`

`MatchEnded`

Payload type: `RlMatchEndedPayload`.

Important fields:

- `MatchGuid?`
- `WinnerTeamNum`

`StatfeedEvent`

Payload type: `RlStatfeedEventPayload`.

Important fields:

- `MatchGuid?`
- `EventName`
- `Type`
- `MainTarget`
- `SecondaryTarget?`

## Fixture Constants And Helpers

`RL_TELEMETRY_FRAME_TEMPLATES`

An object containing one complete sample frame for every supported event.

```ts
const template = RL_TELEMETRY_FRAME_TEMPLATES.GoalScored;
```

Do not mutate templates directly in tests. Use `telemetryFrameTemplate` or the
mock helpers to get a cloned frame.

`telemetryFrameTemplate(eventName)`

Returns a deep-cloned sample frame for an event.

```ts
const frame = telemetryFrameTemplate("UpdateState");
frame.Data.Game.TimeSeconds = 120;
```

`telemetryFrameTemplateJson(eventName)`

Returns a pretty-printed JSON string for a sample frame. This is useful when
building fixture files or inspecting the modeled payload.

```ts
const json = telemetryFrameTemplateJson("GoalScored");
```

`mockRocketLeagueEvent(eventName, overrides)`

Creates a cloned sample frame and shallow-merges `overrides` into `Data`.

```ts
const frame = mockRocketLeagueEvent("ClockUpdatedSeconds", {
  TimeSeconds: 45,
  bOvertime: false
});
```

Event-specific helpers

The SDK also exports one helper per event:

- `mockUpdateState(overrides)`
- `mockBallHit(overrides)`
- `mockClockUpdatedSeconds(overrides)`
- `mockCountdownBegin(overrides)`
- `mockCrossbarHit(overrides)`
- `mockGoalReplayEnd(overrides)`
- `mockGoalReplayStart(overrides)`
- `mockGoalReplayWillEnd(overrides)`
- `mockGoalScored(overrides)`
- `mockMatchCreated(overrides)`
- `mockMatchInitialized(overrides)`
- `mockMatchDestroyed(overrides)`
- `mockMatchEnded(overrides)`
- `mockMatchPaused(overrides)`
- `mockMatchUnpaused(overrides)`
- `mockPodiumStart(overrides)`
- `mockReplayCreated(overrides)`
- `mockReplayWillEnd(overrides)`
- `mockRoundStarted(overrides)`
- `mockStatfeedEvent(overrides)`

`mockUpdateState` merges overrides into `Data.Game`. `mockBallHit` merges
overrides into `Data.Ball`. The other helpers merge overrides into `Data`.

## Typed Subscription Example

```ts
context.bus.subscribe("UpdateState", (event) => {
  const players = event.Data.Players;
  const teams = event.Data.Game.Teams;
  const target = event.Data.Game.Target;
});
```

## Defensive Handling

Telemetry is runtime input. Even when TypeScript knows the expected shape,
plugin code should handle missing optional fields and unexpected values from
external sources.

```ts
context.bus.subscribe("GoalScored", (event) => {
  const scorer = event.Data.Scorer?.Name ?? "Unknown player";
  const assister = event.Data.Assister?.Name ?? null;
});
```
